<p>Insurance claim supplements in Corpus Christi are a normal part of many property claims, not a sign that something went wrong. Adjusters write estimates from what they can see on inspection day, often during a catastrophe workload after a major storm. Once a roofer tears off shingles or a contractor opens a wall, more damage may appear. Code requirements, permit costs, and pricing changes may also be missing from the first estimate. A supplement documents those items and asks the insurer to adjust the claim. Corpus Christi Public Adjuster helps property owners prepare supplements that are specific, supported, and easy for the insurer to evaluate.</p>

<h2>When a Supplement May Be Appropriate</h2>
<p>Common situations include:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Hidden damage found during repairs,</strong> such as deteriorated decking under a hail-damaged roof, wet insulation behind drywall, or water damage under flooring.</li>
<li><strong>Items missed on inspection,</strong> including roof accessories, gutters, fences, detached structures, or entire rooms.</li>
<li><strong>Code and permit requirements</strong> that apply to the repair but were not included.</li>
<li><strong>Quantity corrections,</strong> where measurements or waste factors were too low.</li>
<li><strong>Price changes</strong> between the estimate and the repair, when local costs rose after a storm.</li>
<li><strong>Matching problems,</strong> where repaired areas cannot reasonably match undamaged areas, depending on the policy and facts.</li>
<li><strong>Additional living expense or business income</strong> that ran longer than first expected.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Items Often Missed in Coastal Bend Estimates</h2>
